        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "The accent is part of the meaning",
      "bullets": [
        "<b>hablo</b> (I speak) but <b>habló</b> (he spoke). <b>hablé</b> (I spoke). Without the accent the sentence changes tense or person.",
        "The tú form ends in <b>-ste</b>, never <i>-stes</i>: <b>hablaste</b>, <b>comiste</b>. Only vosotros has the final s: <b>hablasteis</b>.",
        "<b>nosotros -ar and -ir</b> look the same in present and preterite (<i>hablamos</i>, <i>vivimos</i>); the time word decides: <i>Ahora hablamos. Ayer hablamos.</i> The -er verb differs: <i>comemos</i> / <i>comimos</i>."
      ]
    },
